          "preview": "For a binomial count $X \\sim \\mathrm{Bin}(n,p)$, write $X$ as the sum of $n$ independent Bernoulli trials with success probability $p$. Each trial has variance $p(1-p)$, and varian"
        },
        {
          "i": 2,
          "preview": "$$\\mathrm{Var}(X) = np(1-p)$$"
        },
        {
          "i": 3,
          "preview": "This is largest when $p$ is closest to $1/2$, not when $p$ itself is largest."
        },
        {
          "i": 4,
          "preview": "Side A with $n_A = 25$, $p_A = 0.3$:"
        },
        {
          "i": 5,
          "preview": "$$\\mathrm{Var}(A) = 25 \\cdot 0.3 \\cdot 0.7 = 5.25$$"
        },
